    "created_at": "2026-11-23T22:27:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T22:27:37Z",
    "body": "Thank you for this work on Arm64 support. The maintainer decided to decline it for now. The reasons are:\n\n- The `[patch.crates-io]` entry pins Flecs-Rust commit `e7464a8`. That commit is 2 commits after the `0.2.2` tag. It contains the ARM fix (#286), and it also contains the unreleased entity-set refactor (#287). The patch applies on every platform, so x86 builds would also use the unreleased refactor.\n- We cannot build or test aarch64 here. No runner builds it, and `release.yml` does not build it.\n\nYou can propose this change again in one of these two ways:\n1. After `flecs_ecs` 0.2.3 (or a later release with the fix) is on crates.io. Then the change is a normal version bump.\n2. With a patch that adds only the one-line fix of #286 on top of the `0.2.2` tag.\n\nIf you open it again, it gets the priority P6.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
